<h1 local-id=3D"1f4d4214-6fa3-4fc0-a759-cade58dc13be" id=3D"Ignite|R2.1a|SI=
TTestPlan-1.Introduction">1. Introduction</h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"b064326f-bcbe-40a2-8046-62bf7ce623e9" id=3D"Ignite|R2.1a|SI=
TTestPlan-1.1Purpose">1.1 <strong>Purpose</strong></h2>
<p local-id=3D"050ce432-0cb1-4905-aede-e5c3b4397b70">The purpose of this do=
cument is to detail the Test Plan for <span style=3D"color: rgb(0,0,0);">Ig=
nite </span><span style=3D"color: rgb(84,141,212);">- </span><span style=3D=
"color: rgb(0,0,0);">Release 2.1a</span></p>
<p local-id=3D"8c87d519-7c2a-49bc-9817-3a681c1a7e82">This plan will outline=
 how the testing will be conducted, what will be tested, what will not be t=
ested and who will be responsible for the various components of the testing=
.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"479b1ccf-0b80-48bb-8e65-609a38952b17" id=3D"Ignite|R2.1a|SI=
TTestPlan-1.2IntendedAudience"><strong>1.2 Intended Audience </strong></h2>
<p local-id=3D"30eb8325-2010-4990-a3fd-61c906083637">The intended audience =
for this document is:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"3285b702-5205-4958-be13-978ebef2365f">
<li local-id=3D"592e4456-6e4d-49ba-9058-6d600b38e084">
<p local-id=3D"84cd0807-ce4c-4588-9462-278401fe7904">Project Managers</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"e249a9ad-16bf-4c97-97bb-9c5459778667">
<p local-id=3D"917a594e-3280-41fc-8bc0-7c8bbeabdef4">Product Owners</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"266ee500-7235-47f8-a3d9-971689a3643b">
<p local-id=3D"925c111a-dd2c-4ff8-b804-6496712c6ddf">Architects</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"24249a4c-9544-4763-aa3f-6f6e0f7132c3">
<p local-id=3D"fb9f0f53-7b56-4c2d-a3e5-b40b7cdcb8c0">Business Analysts</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"01ccf8c6-2299-4c9d-97ce-53e85578da65">
<p local-id=3D"78503365-c239-4e5f-8310-53365b74a30e">Testing Consultants</p=
>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"a5bf0354-d04c-4962-8d72-83e2bcec1f93" id=3D"Ignite|R2.1a|SI=
TTestPlan-1.3ProjectOverview"><strong>1.3 Project Overview</strong></h2>
<ul local-id=3D"ab3143cd-a4ed-4016-bcfa-f165b00fbefc">
<li local-id=3D"21bdb2d5-68fd-4ec6-a748-b3fe1be3e32f">
<p local-id=3D"b8d9b608-e1cb-42d2-aa5f-083412e91741">The aim of the Campaig=
n Modernisation and Intelligent Decisioning (CMID) project is to transform =
TPG Telecom=E2=80=99s Customer Lifecycle Management capability through:</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"5877c76c-b501-4bc0-ad55-6f578a47b033">
<p local-id=3D"184ca412-68a8-4310-b6f1-30df7637b3cf">Deploying platforms an=
d capabilities that leverage best-in-class Always-On Marketing and Next Bes=
t Action solutions powered by advanced analytics/machine learning models,&n=
bsp;</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"af78c9b8-7c1d-4845-8ccf-1147170bf300">
<p local-id=3D"abe8f544-9b08-4dc9-8236-a9f78b447d12">Delivering personalise=
d, relevant, and highly effective offers and experiences to our customers a=
cross any channel they interact with us,</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"83d2323b-1205-4859-b9cf-030ed880b4b9">
<p local-id=3D"d2d94577-4e36-4c93-a43b-1a144190662c">Optimising both custom=
er experience and commercial outcomes through increased retention, cross-se=
ll and upsell.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"641a80ef-1e19-4911-a729-8a7be195ab1d" id=3D"Ignite|R2.1a|SI=
TTestPlan-1.3.1Belowaresomeofthekeyobjectivesofthisproject:"><strong>1.3.1 =
Below are some of the key objectives of this project:</strong></h3>
<ul local-id=3D"cf6b695c-f748-4192-8135-52952b20d195">
<li local-id=3D"27ac4a1b-00e8-4941-9bbc-73646888870d">
<p local-id=3D"37cc140e-2d3f-4898-83bc-b9ae192e09cc">Ingestion of Real-Time=
 data &amp; Insights around customers and their interactions into the marke=
ting platform.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"fda1ba88-3c02-4785-ab1d-e8742775b27b">
<p local-id=3D"ccff60f2-74ed-4a34-81c3-5173ba42f8bb">Using all available da=
ta points and triggers to make effective marketing decisions =E2=80=93 auto=
mated, timely and at scale.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"a1bcc597-d252-4749-bfb0-f1d0966a2b1f">
<p local-id=3D"57b13cfc-24da-4e9b-9581-7cbfc1ab6dcb">Creating feedback loop=
s into the decisioning engine to enable continuous optimisation driven by a=
dvanced analytics and machine learning.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"b1ff6b21-4b6b-4cce-bf8b-9cf74f989853">
<p local-id=3D"be3ea407-f855-4676-b376-cd674057599c">Building marketing pla=
tforms that are flexible and responsive to the constant market changes.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"01382221-7b63-4ed3-88be-d3fc4d86a10f">
<p local-id=3D"67f92f1b-387c-4a1b-9a14-93a023e8d333">Seamlessly integrate t=
he decisioning and recommendations into all channels to improve customer ex=
perience and conversion.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"40bafc35-c9e3-438c-b833-dfa7a368a514">
<p local-id=3D"cbee8eec-8f1e-421e-89ea-c80d48fd5eb8">This ABTL (Automated B=
elow The Line) initiative will allow the business to have a single source o=
f truth for storing all products and rewards as well as a robust framework =
for automated fulfillment of these bundled or standalone through assisted a=
nd un-assisted channels. This program in conjunction with the centralised d=
ecisioning engine (Pega CDH) will improve customer experience, and will ena=
ble customers to receive real time strategic offers that will reduce churn =
and increase revenue. Building a framework to support offering bespoke offe=
rs to existing customers is a key driver for a successful retention program=
</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"4b4d6eea-42b3-43fe-9cf4-eaf3ca1d3ae5" id=3D"Ignite|R2.1a|SI=
TTestPlan-1.3.2IgniteR2.1aSolutionEnhancements:"><strong>1.3.2 Ignite R2.1a=
 Solution Enhancements: </strong></h3>
<p local-id=3D"796f0a92-52bf-4485-a631-e1c4ec7c917d">R2.1a addresses a set =
of design gaps, fulfilment inconsistencies, and new requirements raised aft=
er the R2 SAD was baselined. These items emerged through:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"2509fc69-3a8f-4272-a66a-3cd2e3548e0b">
<li local-id=3D"60c9b78f-88da-4d98-965b-f5df90929c4e">
<p local-id=3D"e372e64a6129">R2 Open Items</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"bd4cc840-b447-4ee0-a9ca-db8286f7d5b7">
<p local-id=3D"990290d3f888">R2.1 Kanban board</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"44ffd03a-98e2-4b0e-9fec-d6d2cacf1e4d">
<p local-id=3D"6c8b3d90c147">Siebel SSJ/F Interlock Alignment</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"b34f0845-00b8-4847-9df6-45a45cfa262c" id=3D"Ignite|R2.1a|SI=
TTestPlan-1.3.3KeyobjectivesofIgniteR2.1ainclude:"><strong>1.3.3 Key object=
ives of Ignite R2.1a include:</strong></h3>
<p local-id=3D"8f6e5ea1-64a0-4bd1-ac2f-657329ffbd62">R2.1a enhances the R2 =
solution across Decisioning (Pega CDH), Siebel SSJ fulfilment, and downstre=
am layers. The focus is on:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"28cbcce1acae">
<li local-id=3D"a61481f45581">
<p local-id=3D"5b9bc60b77d0">Expanding ATL/BTL offer handling.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"b0bdb0e47108">
<p local-id=3D"ee041d31aaab">Standardising discount logic and FixedDiscount=
 behaviour.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"b803e7e9be59">
<p local-id=3D"64e6347b0f95">Improving some offer types handling (Content, =
Credit Governance).</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"eefe2c62b38e">
<p local-id=3D"cf0a58840b0a">Improving missed-offer handling and bulk provi=
sioning.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"976ed0ffa20e">
<p local-id=3D"806fe1155deb">Strengthening fulfilment consistency across R1=
/R2 agents.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"1d47bd313dfe">
<p local-id=3D"641eeaebe2f6">Enabling channel-specific behaviour (Single Pr=
ice Per Plan).</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"1901f7e2c9b5">
<p local-id=3D"4fe9562397a3">Streamlining agent workflows with Siebel Open =
UI for a unified interface.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"6e71023cc747">
<p local-id=3D"2221e64a92e0">Seamless integration between Pega CDH and Sieb=
el Open UI for real-time decisioning.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"cdba624c2c6c">
<p local-id=3D"def87037f6d5"><span style=3D"background-color: rgb(253,208,2=
36);">Express fulfillment, Go to sales calculator via SSJ quote &amp; fulfi=
llment along with Ignite offers.</span></p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"1d82a4a3a4ad">
<p local-id=3D"6691d4a16233">Seamless integration across Care centre and Re=
tail stores.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"13c985864d62">
<p local-id=3D"10bc6b659ec9">Expanding cross-sell and bundling use cases.</=
p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"e86e3a1be1d1">
<p local-id=3D"b7ff9b09f653">Flexibility in choosing bundles &amp; add-ons.=
</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"3f8fcfc7f0a8">
<p local-id=3D"6b4763f79a14">Personalized product recommendations based on =
real time data.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"fec0ec19f40c">
<p local-id=3D"76d5587927c8">Scalable &amp; adaptable decisioning.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"f41bef00086f">
<p local-id=3D"2e9f21cd411c">Data driven cross-selling strategies leading h=
igh conversion rates.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"53152d6c28f0">
<p local-id=3D"6e7dd9663dec">Aligning with the Target Data Architecture (TD=
A) for consistent data processing.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"ff3e2ff06af6">
<p local-id=3D"a511d2ae30c2">Ensuring end-to-end data security and complian=
ce.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"0df7cb94266c">
<p local-id=3D"20d211732ae5">This solution aims to provide a comprehensive,=
 automated approach to customer interactions, improving efficiency and cons=
istency.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"869506f42409">
<p local-id=3D"65e045e06787">Enhancing dynamic Customer Intent.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"ae91a8a388e9">
<p local-id=3D"cf312b213241">Improving auditability and reporting.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"98c0d8c4b515">
<p local-id=3D"d94a346a6603"><span style=3D"background-color: rgb(253,208,2=
36);">Pause &amp; Resume functionality , Bulk Provisioning, Pick and Mix co=
mpatibility will be tested once Siebel solution completed and delivered to =
SIT. </span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"68c50b949fc6">R2.1a does <strong>not</strong> introduce new =
integration patterns.</p>
<p local-id=3D"345e190de1aa">Overall, R2.1a is an <strong>incremental updat=
e to enable GTM</strong> =E2=80=94 designed to strengthen fulfilment consis=
tency, improve visibility, and extend offer decisioning coverage, or major =
architectural shifts. R2.1a introduces <strong>Container API V2</strong> to=
 support non-breaking schema changes related to Request payload (AgentDetai=
ls, CreditCheckDetails and Contexts) restructuring.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c341f4057d09">R2.1a will consume data from the Teradata =E2=
=86=92 GDM =E2=86=92 AL/CIC =E2=86=92 Pega CDH,</p>
<span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper conflu=
ence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image image-ce=
nter" alt=3D"0e0ae55c-80e4-4dba-a8e3-2fbf1864bd8b.png" width=3D"468" loadin=
g=3D"lazy" src=3D"30aa75b1a272e7c3898615ae8bafbcd3f9571d1498eb09a18ae0d63dd=
ee287ae" data-image-src=3D"https://tpgtelecom.atlassian.net/wiki/download/a=
ttachments/9402009583628/0e0ae55c-80e4-4dba-a8e3-2fbf1864bd8b.png?version=
=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1778587527489&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2=
" data-height=3D"759" data-width=3D"1236" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"=
0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"9402042320415" data-linked-resource-version=
=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-defaul=
t-alias=3D"0e0ae55c-80e4-4dba-a8e3-2fbf1864bd8b.png" data-base-url=3D"https=
://tpgtelecom.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"imag=
e/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"9402009583628" data-linked-reso=
urce-container-version=3D"8" data-media-id=3D"5585ee31-81ae-488e-88f2-bac2d=
58a0eb0" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"287"></span>
<p local-id=3D"d0d664ac4766" style=3D"text-align: center;"><span style=3D"c=
olor: rgb(23,43,77);">Figure1 : <span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-=
ref=3D"e4f70bdf-b703-4e1f-8566-901139a99036">Release 2.1A Solution Architec=
ture Diagram</span></span></p>
<p local-id=3D"a7342775c05d" style=3D"text-align: center;"><strong>*The dia=
gram reflects the originally planned data source changes for the Ignite pro=
gram. Due to delays in the Illuminate implementation, the decision has been=
 made to use the existing production data source for Release 2. As a result=
, the diagram does not accurately represent the current data source approac=
h*</strong></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"a8adf2da-6059-420c-b5ff-b643e4f8a939" id=3D"Ignite|R2.1a|SI=
TTestPlan-2.SolutionOverview">2. Solution Overview</h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"5f5ba599-ae1a-4691-a3c1-82df526e9b3e" id=3D"Ignite|R2.1a|SI=
TTestPlan-2.1In-Scope(IgniteR2.1a):"><strong>2.1 <span class=3D"inline-comm=
ent-marker" data-ref=3D"b908c538-53f3-4e63-9759-e69a61c4c040">In-Scope (Ign=
ite R2.1a) </span>:</strong></h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"fcd0bb97f65c" id=3D"Ignite|R2.1a|SITTestPlan-2.1.1NewRequir=
ements:">2.1.1 <span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"c0fa6e6e-7=
99e-4c13-90bb-23dfcaf096c1">New Requirements</span>:</h3>
<p local-id=3D"7d322940c8fb"><strong>CLMNBA-3568 - Ability to Recommend Fix=
ed Discounts Independent of Contract Duration</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"b975879d5a19">
<li local-id=3D"2e271929c79c">
<p local-id=3D"148947d8fd39">This capability enables Pega to recommend ATL =
(Above The Line) and BTL (Below The Line) offers where the total discount a=
mount is fixed (e.g., $400 off), regardless of the contract duration select=
ed by the customer.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"e74c27beaf59">
<p local-id=3D"9f66107212f9">The monthly repayment is calculated by dividin=
g the discounted total price by the selected term, allowing for minor round=
ing differences.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"e46b58f95861"><strong>CLMNBA-3852 - Enhance Container API to=
 include Dealer and Channel Context Attributes</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"ebe356125945">
<li local-id=3D"29181bf82979">
<p local-id=3D"53a128bc8571">Currently, only <em>RetailDealerCode</em> is i=
ncluded in the Container API request. To provide richer sales context, the =
API will be enhanced to include <em>SalesChannel</em> (e.g., Retail, Online=
, DMP) and <em>DealerGroup</em> (e.g., Smart Phones, TeleChoice).</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"0cf6477124a8">
<p local-id=3D"bbd969038ed6">These attributes will be sourced from Siebel d=
ealer metadata and will be used by Pega for data enrichment (IH/DH extracts=
) and future decisioning enhancements.
<br>
There are no changes to decisioning logic or response contract for R2.1; th=
is is purely contextual enablement.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"20c2fd45e954"><strong>CLMNBA-3630 - Credit recommendation</s=
trong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"627eed0b-0972-48ab-aa6d-0c6dfff7b5fb">
<li local-id=3D"219ea23e-5c01-482e-86ff-7d42a5a1cde4">
<p local-id=3D"87555a2da61f">In R1, agents issued one-off account credits (=
e.g., $30) via manual adjustments outside the cart flow; Pega only recommen=
ded them.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"06c17bddd640">
<p local-id=3D"1101c41d3760">In R2, fulfilment journeys live in Siebel/SSJ/=
TBUI and there is no direct cart journey for credits. Credits are also not =
cart-based, which limits the Pega feedback loop and learnings.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"a8e8eb3aca17"><strong>CLMNBA-3854 - Ensure consistent tracki=
ng of all Pega-recommended offers (Type 0=E2=80=933) in Siebel for reportin=
g and attribution</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"63067239d300">
<li local-id=3D"93c9564886ac">
<p local-id=3D"53c411dda694">Currently, Type 0 (ATL) offers provided by Peg=
a CDH are not captured in Siebel=E2=80=99s CX_Offer_History with their asso=
ciated Interaction ID, leading to partial visibility of Pega=E2=80=99s cont=
ribution in offer reporting.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"0337640b10e2">
<p local-id=3D"8e1798a002e1">While Types 1=E2=80=933 are already tracked co=
rrectly, the absence of consistent tagging for Type 0 creates reporting and=
 attribution gaps across fulfillment and downstream analytics layers (MDS/I=
lluminate).</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"cb45e950f8ec">
<p local-id=3D"4b8c838c1f93">Additionally, offers that are not driven by Pe=
ga =E2=80=94 such as those added manually in SSJ =E2=80=94 should be explic=
itly excluded from Pega attribution by ensuring they do not carry a Pega_In=
teraction_ID and their offer_source =E2=89=A0 'Pega'.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"b08d0a348f7a">
<p local-id=3D"4072ef8c2eaf">To make the framework future-proof, this story=
 standardises offer tagging across all offer types and ensures that any Peg=
a-originated recommendation =E2=80=94 irrespective of the offer channel or =
fulfillment type =E2=80=94 carries the correct attribution metadata.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"0817c3073d61"><strong>CLMNBA-3570 - Type 1 Offer inclusion i=
n Decisioning &amp; Offer Tiles</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"7068fa9e9fad">
<li local-id=3D"04de9210d9c0">
<p local-id=3D"0a62140f5dd4">This capability enables Pega to recognise and =
transmit Type 1 ATL inclusions (e.g., extra data, IDD minutes, ATL price ad=
justments) so they can be used in engagement policy and arbitration and cle=
arly displayed on offer tiles (for example, in the =E2=80=9Coffers=E2=80=9D=
 section or equivalent channel widget).</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"245f120584ed">
<p local-id=3D"2aedb3ca9966">Pega applies transient overlay attributes befo=
re engagement policy and arbitration, ensuring conditional ATL (e.g., =E2=
=80=9Cnew services only=E2=80=9D) is evaluated correctly and presented cons=
istently across channels.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"30c0e09edfde"><strong>CLMNBA-3650 - Offer Section for recomm=
endations</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"59eb117dd2dc">
<li local-id=3D"7541f0583a47">
<p local-id=3D"0797898df747">Recommendations may include additional inclusi=
ons beyond the standard plan benefits (e.g., =E2=80=9C20GB Extra Data=E2=80=
=9D, =E2=80=9C100 Z1 Minutes=E2=80=9D).</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"92ed07deb837">
<p local-id=3D"132bb5d677cf">These inclusions can be Above=E2=80=91the=E2=
=80=91Line (ATL) or Below=E2=80=91the=E2=80=91Line (BTL). Pega will supply =
these items concatenated in a single field named WhyRelevant<strong> </stro=
ng>at the parent action level, with each inclusion separated by a pipe (<co=
de>|</code>).</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"771dd43a5176">
<p local-id=3D"98b9717002a6">The UI must split and present these items on t=
he offer section tile, in a dedicated area outside the standard Benefits li=
st.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"789d5a496649"><strong>CLMNBA-3798 - Add on Inclusion in Reco=
mmendations (RPC/Upgrade &amp; Standalone)</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"90e09ec78395">
<li local-id=3D"b4c2a601b57d">
<p local-id=3D"42edf74726ca">The business requires flexibility to offer add=
-ons either bundled with a plan/contract change or independently, allowing =
customers to receive tailored benefits.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"4a4c91eedeca">
<p local-id=3D"93bc00482da9">Add-ons may be free rewards (no price) or disc=
ounted in-market add-ons (AU Code + Discount).</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"ef7c118de516">
<p local-id=3D"c041fd05eb33">The capability must handle all combinations=E2=
=80=94RPC, Upgrade, and Standalone=E2=80=94ensuring correct payload constru=
ction, fulfilment integration, and UI clarity.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"a7ebfa54f23b"><strong>CLMNBA-3649-Credit offer lifecycle</st=
rong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"7ddfde5a2d47">
<li local-id=3D"c5f8601251d9">
<p local-id=3D"40d29590ad75">Credits (discounts) with a duration longer tha=
n one month may remain active across plan changes and service events.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"e99380825862">
<p local-id=3D"59e299105d94">We need clear, deterministic rules for when a =
credit is kept or dropped after each event, so agents and customers experie=
nce consistent outcomes and billing remains correct.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"5fc09af34bfe"><strong>CLMNBA -3867 BUS - Offer Lifecycle Man=
agement for Type 3 Offers</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"d47ac329-11dd-4237-9c02-b8fab8ed20b2">
<li local-id=3D"ee55ae71-96ac-449c-b9e4-2d01a2db029f">
<p local-id=3D"0102975c869f">Type 3 offers are BTL (below-the-line) rewards=
 generated by Pega and fulfilled through Siebel. When customers change serv=
ice status (e.g., suspend, reactivate, transfer ownership), Pega must evalu=
ate whether to retain, reinstate, or remove the associated offers to ensure=
 accuracy of discounts and prevent benefit misuse.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"e597d4c38837"><strong>CLMNBA-3659 - Stackability and Co-exis=
tence</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"7b1b43c2a2cb">
<li local-id=3D"7be784396879">
<p local-id=3D"31116538519c">We are standardizing how offers being recommen=
ded at the same time can sit together (stack) and whether a newly accepted =
offer should keep or replace an existing one on the same service (co=E2=80=
=91existence).</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"9fb37afe7c40">
<p local-id=3D"92439f2694ae">Stackability is simplified to default behaviou=
rs, removing the need for an explicit flag. This aligns the experience acro=
ss ATL/BTL.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"1b4b20861f65"><strong>CLMNBA-3664 - Order Compliance until f=
ulfilment</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"2b3799faf2d1">
<li local-id=3D"6ac5d8b77f33">
<p local-id=3D"fe123be6d9f7">We must prevent invalid combinations (e.g., a =
plan-only discount that actually requires a device) while keeping the UI re=
sponsive.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"7da1a459f5fc"><strong>CLMNBA-4978 -Order Compliance until fu=
lfilment</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"dd279b50-a1f2-4a55-a8e8-6df114a5948b">
<li local-id=3D"59cfc0bc-9229-4bd8-973a-2043c91a775b">
<p local-id=3D"a84d08cde7e9">To ensure all compatibility rules where a plan=
 or discount depends on a device. The system must prevent agents from fulfi=
lling invalid or incompatible combinations during recommendation journey, e=
nsuring:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"67cc34c2-c6b2-46ab-bc02-5510ff98e959">
<li local-id=3D"19f961f7-6f20-463e-886a-42bccc2f9447">
<p local-id=3D"5b5f15864c5b">A plans requiring a device cannot be fulfilled=
 standalone</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"c5907d0a-ae77-4902-8f74-c004567d539a">
<p local-id=3D"aea1d9f25c6c">Device=E2=80=91linked discounts remain valid o=
nly when the required device is present</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"e7117413-4711-4c58-bc73-547f75c67514">
<p local-id=3D"5c2e572b70ab">Removing or swapping the device triggers autom=
atic removal of dependent offers</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"153d914c-0115-4b3e-b53b-bcbafcd2ecdc">
<p local-id=3D"4804d8a9a20c">Validation must be real-time to enforce all ru=
les (listed in ACs)</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"1d09164b-cb0c-4bb5-a66a-c7136fa913e1">
<p local-id=3D"8e4a0664a2f8">The most restrictive rule between Pega and Sie=
bel must always apply</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"32ef1987-0fee-4f70-9c0e-97d860fce302">
<p local-id=3D"b179f8993da6">Checkout must be blocked until all dependencie=
s are satisfied</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"dcd06d438ad1"><strong>CLMNBA-4900 - Enforce =E2=80=9CApplica=
ble Quantity=E2=80=9D for New Service Offers in Pick &amp; Mix</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"b19b7f398416">
<li local-id=3D"1321ffca6f59">
<p local-id=3D"977174475055">Certain offers must be capped so customers or =
agents cannot add unlimited quantities of the same offer into the cart.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"71de8bd65291"><strong>CLMNBA - 5460 NBN Template changes - I=
gnite Implementation- Business Continuity</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"546be3a509e6">
<li local-id=3D"27a3c7b60a5a">
<p local-id=3D"7edc4101c816">As NBN rolls out new generation FTTP/HFC Netwo=
rk Termination Devices (NTDs) and updates its APIs, Siebel will receive add=
itional and updated attributes (e.g., <code>ntdType</code>, <code>ntdVersio=
n</code>, <code>speedTiersSupported</code>, <code>NTDBandwidth</code>,<code=
>resourceMas</code>) from NBN. While Siebel will manage these changes withi=
n its existing projects, this requirement ensures that all new attributes a=
re passed downstream to Pega and handled seamlessly, without requiring work=
flow modifications.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"db340718faaf"><strong>CLMNBA -3591 Bus -Content Offers</stro=
ng></p>
<ul local-id=3D"480eb2a27484">
<li local-id=3D"f595a06a297a">
<p local-id=3D"968d1d07dff8">Content offers are a differentiator rather tha=
n a core revenue stream; fulfilment and billing sit outside Siebel (e.g., v=
ia third parties).Today, voucher campaigns allocate and send codes after el=
igible orders, and redemption/active user reports are received periodically=
. Ignite (outbound) will need the content acceptance signal to drive vouche=
r campaigns when enabled; until then, campaigns may continue on legacy tool=
ing. Decisioning should present content add=E2=80=91ins consistently and re=
cord them as part of the accepted offer payload for downstream use.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"a47802fdc56d"><strong>CLMNBA -3894 BUS - Fulfilment Monitori=
ng Requirements</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"e594168ab6cb">
<li local-id=3D"59a61d80c7d4">
<p local-id=3D"ac5dff2a747a">This capability covers the scenarios where off=
ers may behave incorrectly due to agent actions, system or integration issu=
es such as:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"e9db3d4d27cb">
<li local-id=3D"b8587b7c25f1">
<p local-id=3D"bd4fca38dc2c">Offers applied to the wrong service or MSISDN<=
/p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"462cf63171bd">
<p local-id=3D"c31b9e71b6e4">Discounts continuing after service cancellatio=
n</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"124bc1df31f6">
<p local-id=3D"a845d74cd6cb">Incorrect offer restoration during reactivatio=
n or ownership change</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"b42c249efd48">
<p local-id=3D"337da20de28e">Violations of stackability and coexistence rul=
es</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"7fc89261fc10">
<p local-id=3D"27a797654807">Cart validation failures (e.g., missing device=
, invalid contract term)</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
